---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="MotionHotel privacy policy template."
  ><section class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p><h1>Simple and respectful.</h1><p>
      A clear template for explaining how your hotel website handles personal
      information.
    </p>
  </section><section class="section prose legal-prose">
    <p class="legal-notice">
      Theme template only — tailor this policy to your actual tools, hosting,
      booking provider and legal jurisdiction. It is not legal advice.
    </p><h2>Controller</h2><p>
      [Company / Hotel name]<br />[Address]<br />[Email address]<br />[Phone
      number]
    </p><h2>Website hosting and server logs</h2><p>
      When visitors access this website, the hosting provider may process
      technically necessary server log data such as IP address, date and time,
      requested page and browser information. Add the identity of your host,
      purpose, legal basis and retention period here.
    </p><h2>Reservations and contact requests</h2><p>
      When a visitor submits the contact form, the website sends their name,
      email address and message to the contact inbox by email. The form does not
      store submissions in a website database. The website host and mail
      provider may process the submission and email as part of delivering the
      message. Update this section to identify your host, mail provider and
      retention practices, and to cover any booking provider or other contact
      tools you use.
    </p><h2>Spam protection</h2><p>
      When a contact or booking request is submitted, this site uses Google
      reCAPTCHA v3 to help detect automated abuse. Google may process device,
      browser, IP address and interaction information. Google's
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms">Terms of Service</a> apply.
      Update this policy with the applicable legal basis and retention details.
    </p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>
      Depending on applicable law, visitors may have rights of access,
      correction, deletion, restriction, objection and data portability, as well
      as the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
    </p><h2>Third-party services</h2><p>
      List every analytics, map, embedded social media, newsletter or booking
      service used on the live site. This static demo does not include analytics
      or tracking by default.
    </p>
  </section></BaseLayout
>
